8|0@SandersForPresident^1440085534#cu9kkh6:Vermonter_Here$:There's a general consensus among Vermonter that beyond his policy positions, he genuinely cares, and genuinely listens to the needs of people here. Some estimate that about half our state have heard him speak, or spoken to him personally (I count myself twice on that latter point). We have a lot of farms in Vermont, and farmers tend to be socially conservative. But Bernie recognizes them, and recognizes that they're important. And the farmers look back and see someone who cares. The only people who don't support him in our state are those who have a fundamental disagreement with him on principle of his identifying as a socialist. Everyone else gets it: he cares. And this is why we'll win this election. He's an excellent campaigner, and he campaigns on his ideas. It just so happens that his ideas actually *help* people, and when people hear him speak, they often realize this.
